---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import '../styles/company.css';
---
<BaseLayout title="Contact" description="Reach Chudware directly: sales, support, security disclosure, privacy, and legal, each on its own address, plus self-serve documentation and FAQ.">
  <header class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Contact</p>
      <h1>Five addresses, each read by a person.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Pick the route that matches the question. Mail sent to the right address is answered faster than mail routed through a general inbox, and there is no ticket robot in between.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="co-routes">
    <div class="wrap">
      <header class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Direct routes</p>
        <h2 id="co-routes" class="co-anchor">Where to send what.</h2>
      </header>
      <div class="co-routes">
        <article class="co-route" data-lift>
          <p class="eyebrow">Sales</p>
          <h3>Access, seats, and deployment</h3>
          <p>Multiple seats, organization access, native Windows or Linux preview builds, or a commercial question while the public rate card is being finalized.</p>
          <a class="co-route-address" href="mailto:sales@chudware.com?subject=Chudware%20access">sales@chudware.com</a>
        </article>
        <article class="co-route" data-lift>
          <p class="eyebrow">Support</p>
          <h3>Something is not working</h3>
          <p>Sign-in trouble, an account stuck awaiting approval, a workspace that will not open, a copilot run that fails, or billing that looks wrong.</p>
          <a class="co-route-address" href="mailto:support@chudware.com?subject=Chudware%20support">support@chudware.com</a>
        </article>
        <article class="co-route co-route-urgent" data-lift>
          <p class="eyebrow">Security</p>
          <h3>Vulnerability disclosure</h3>
          <p>Include the affected surface, the impact, and reproduction steps. Test only against your own account and data. No bug bounty, no formal response-time commitment, read by the engineers.</p>
          <a class="co-route-address" href="mailto:security@chudware.com?subject=Security%20report">security@chudware.com</a>
        </article>
        <article class="co-route" data-lift>
          <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
          <h3>Your data</h3>
          <p>Review account data, revoke sessions and devices, remove provider keys, export project files, or request account deletion.</p>
          <a class="co-route-address" href="mailto:privacy@chudware.com?subject=Privacy%20request">privacy@chudware.com</a>
        </article>
        <article class="co-route" data-lift>
          <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
          <h3>Terms and agreements</h3>
          <p>Questions about the terms of service, the EULA, or the refund policy.</p>
          <a class="co-route-address" href="mailto:legal@chudware.com?subject=Legal%20question">legal@chudware.com</a>
        </article>
        <article class="co-route" data-lift>
          <p class="eyebrow">Anything else</p>
          <h3>General enquiry</h3>
          <p>If none of the above fits, sales is the general front door and will pass the message to whoever should answer it.</p>
          <a class="co-route-address" href="mailto:sales@chudware.com?subject=Chudware%20enquiry">sales@chudware.com</a>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="co-self">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div>
        <header class="section-heading">
          <p class="eyebrow">Faster than mail</p>
          <h2 id="co-self" class="co-anchor">Most first questions are already answered.</h2>
        </header>
        <ul class="co-selfserve">
          <li><a class="text-link" href="/faq/">FAQ</a><p>Browser versus native, platforms, file formats, where files live, copilot and API keys, commercial status.</p></li>
          <li><a class="text-link" href="/docs/">Documentation</a><p>Sketching, first part, assemblies, CAM, PLM, the copilot, keyboard reference, and troubleshooting.</p></li>
          <li><a class="text-link" href="/security/">Security</a><p>What the gateway enforces, the parameters behind it, and the assurances Chudware does not claim.</p></li>
          <li><a class="text-link" href="/pricing/">Pricing</a><p>Why no rate card is published yet, and the routes that are open in the meantime.</p></li>
          <li><a class="text-link" href="/download/">Access</a><p>Start in the browser now, or request a native Windows or Linux preview build.</p></li>
          <li><a class="text-link" href="/changelog/">Changelog</a><p>What actually shipped, rather than what is planned.</p></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="co-aside">
        <div class="co-note" data-lift>
          <p class="eyebrow">Make the mail useful</p>
          <p>For a support message, say which route you are on (browser client or native preview), the account address, what you did, and what happened instead. For a security report, reproduction steps beat severity adjectives.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="co-noform" data-lift>
          <p><strong>There is no contact form here, on purpose.</strong></p>
          <p>Every address above goes to a person, not a queue. A plain address is honest, works from any mail client, and leaves you holding a copy of exactly what you sent.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section cta-band">
    <div class="wrap section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Or skip the conversation</p>
      <h2>Open the product and judge it directly.</h2>
      <p class="lede">A browser account takes less time than writing the email asking whether it is any good.</p>
      <div class="actions"><a class="button" href="https://app.chudware.com/signup">Create an account</a><a class="button button-secondary" href="/about/">About Chudware</a></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
